<title>SPAIN: Amper plans nominal cut, 200 ptas payback.</title>
<headline>Amper plans nominal cut, 200 ptas payback.</headline>
<dateline>MADRID 1997-06-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Spanish phone equipment group Amper's board is proposing a nominal share value reduction to 300 from 500 pesetas, returning the 200 pta per share difference to shareholders, a company spokesman said on Tuesday.  </p>
<p>In addition, the board approved a dividend of 85 pesetas, of which a 45 peseta interim dividend has already been paid.</p>
<p>--Madrid Newsroom +34 1 585 2167</p>
</text>
